#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:64
msgid ""
"All of the above functions can accept an additional options argument that"
" is an object that can contain one or more of the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:66
msgid "`scheme` (string)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:68
msgid ""
"Indicates the scheme that the URI should be treated as, overriding the "
"URI's normal scheme parsing behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:70
msgid "`reference` (string)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:72
msgid ""
"If set to `\"suffix\"`, it indicates that the URI is in the suffix "
"format, and the validator will use the option's `scheme` property to "
"determine the URI's scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:74
msgid "`tolerant` (boolean, false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:76
msgid "If set to `true`, the parser will relax URI resolving rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:78
msgid "`absolutePath` (boolean, false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:80
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the serializer will not resolve a relative `path` "
"component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:82
msgid "`iri` (boolean, false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:84
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the serializer will unescape non-ASCII characters as "
"per [RFC 3987](http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3987.txt)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:86
msgid "`unicodeSupport` (boolean, false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:88
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the parser will unescape non-ASCII characters in the "
"parsed output as per [RFC 3987](http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3987.txt)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:90
msgid "`domainHost` (boolean, false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uri-js_README.md:92
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the library will treat the `host` component as a domain"
" name, and convert IDNs (International Domain Names) as per [RFC "
"5891](http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc5891.txt)."
msgstr ""

